A Classifier under Alien Skies
==============================

Open index.html directly (file://), or serve it beside TeachingTools. Native
offline HTML/Canvas/JavaScript; no Shiny, WebR, CDN, modules or installation.
app.R and model.R remain unchanged retained reference sources.

Principle: validation only represents its measurement/deployment conditions.
Two Gaussian colour populations have means (+/-0.8,+/-0.4), independent SDs
0.35 and 0.45, and equal class frequencies. A source LDA is trained on 400
objects using sample class means and the average within-class sample covariance.
Both independent validation samples contain 400 objects, 200 per class. Target
colours add (offset,0.4*offset) and independent Gaussian noise per colour.
The source classifier uses equal priors and assigns exact boundary ties to 0.

Frozen source; honest correction
--------------------------------
Source training, source validation, intrinsic target colours and standardised
target noise are cached by seed. Target offset/noise, view and adaptation
changes NEVER regenerate or refit source training. Truth is used only for
accuracy, class styling and error rings, never target adaptation.

The original uncorrected rule is retained. Added optional comparisons:
* Known external calibration subtracts the specified simulated offset, as an
  idealised independent-calibration benchmark. This uses known calibration
  information, not target labels, and does not remove measurement noise.
* Unlabelled mean alignment subtracts mean(target features)-mean(source training
  features), without any class labels. Evaluation on that same unlabelled batch
  is transductive. It assumes a shared class mixture and an additive shift;
  sample fluctuations, changed class proportions or complex shifts can harm it.

Explain explicitly distinguishes domain/measurement shift from the narrower
pure-covariate-shift assumption, and warns that choosing a correction using
displayed target accuracies tunes on validation labels. An actual deployment
needs a separate final test set. This balanced toy is not a realistic quasar
survey; decision-region shading is a class, not a correctness probability.

Native differences
------------------
Preserves all original controls, presets, LDA equations, population sizes,
original/new-survey comparison and lecture link. Adds the optional corrections,
side-by-side accuracy metrics and per-class validation error counts. Plots keep
common axes between original/target views. No animation (the comparison is
static). New realisation advances a seeded Astro RNG; Reset restores defaults.
R/browser RNG streams differ, but fixed-data LDA agrees with retained-R fixtures.

Numerical API (model.js, browser SurveyShiftModel and CommonJS)
-------------------------------------------------------------
defaults; SIZE=400; validate(parameters)
fitClassifier(twoColourRows, binaryLabels)
  -> weight, threshold, class means, pooled covariance
predict(model, twoColourRows, correction=[0,0]) -> binary predictions
calibrationCorrection(trainingRows, targetRows, mode, knownOffset)
  -> two-coordinate correction; modes none / known / unlabelled; no target labels
accuracy(predictions, labels) -> fraction correct
prepare(seed) -> fixed source/target base samples, source fit and validation
compute(parameters, optionalPrepared) -> target observations, frozen/corrected
  predictions, correction, and all independent validation accuracies
Rows are [colour1,colour2]. Invalid values and singular training covariance
throw Astro.ValidationError. Parameters: seed integer 0..2147483647, offset
-2..2, noise 0..1.2, view target/original, adaptation none/known/unlabelled.

Validation (from the repository root)
------------------------------------
node SurveyShift/test_model.js
node SurveyShift/test_browser.js
Tests use retained-R LDA fixtures including strict boundary ties, relabelling,
fixed source data, matched/shifted validation limits, exact calibration recovery,
irreducible noise, target-label invariance, offset-equivariant mean alignment,
seed stability, singular covariance and boundaries. Chrome additionally checks
decision regions, error rings, metrics/table, all choices, mobile and file://.
For a repository-local Chrome profile, create SurveyShift/.browser-state, set
TMPDIR to its absolute path for the test, then remove the empty directory.

Runtime assets: index.html, model.js, app.js, plus
../TeachingTools/{statistics.js,browser.js,browser.css,lesson.js}. No others.
